 Record design decisions, hypotheses, review findings, and unresolved questions here.
 Imported associated notes retain original evidence/timestamps in `evidence/associated_notes.jsonl`.
+
+## Current reviewer finding — aligned bounding-box lane shortcut
+
+Review `review-d54ac4e249fb35e7` left production source unchanged and added a
+source-pinned Racket probe. Across 64 generated inputs (32 horizontal and 32
+vertical), the plausible wrong rule “paint the entire one-cell lane between the
+two groups' bounding boxes” matched the selected canonical output 64/64 times.
+The sampler always emits aligned, equal-length two-cell bars, so that shortcut
+collapses to the intended one-step plus-growth intersection.
+
+A lawful 8×8 diagnostic accepted by the current `self_check` offsets two
+three-cell bars by one row. Protected Racket paints only contact cells `(2,2)`
+and `(3,2)`; the shortcut also paints `(1,2)` and `(4,2)`. The exact input,
+outputs, source/rule hashes, and 65 Racket evaluations are retained in
+`counterexamples/bbox_lane_shortcut.json`; the reusable probe and regression are
+`workspace/probe_bbox_lane_shortcut.py` and
+`tests/test_bbox_lane_shortcut_probe.py`.
+
+A concrete repair is to add unequal-length or offset groups constructively,
+strengthen `self_check` to verify the stated gap/contact invariants, register the
+bounding-box-lane rival, and require each released lesson to reject it. Until
+then the task remains an audit finding, not a reviewed-safe generator repair.
