+## Current reviewer finding — top/left tie-precedence ambiguity
+
+Review `review-d54ac4e249fb35e7` left the accepted v3.0.2 source unchanged and
+added one undeclared plausible rival: sort equal occupied-area bodies by
+bounding-box **left before top**, rather than the intended top before left. On
+the ordinary seed-0 window at indices 4–9, that rival matches all five visible
+Racket labels at indices 4–8 but disagrees with query index 9 in seven cells.
+The query contains two five-cell bodies at `(top,left)=(6,4)` and `(8,1)`, so
+top-first and left-first choose opposite orders.
+
+The exact six protected-Racket labels, input, outputs, source/rule hashes, and
+cell differences are retained in
+`counterexamples/left_before_top_ambiguity.json`; the reusable probe and
+regression are `workspace/probe_left_before_top.py` and
+`tests/test_left_before_top_ambiguity.py`.
+
+The next repair is constructive: every five-demo lesson needs an equal-area
+example where top order conflicts with left order, and `left_before_top` should
+be added to `LESSON_COMPETITORS` before rerunning all query rotations. Existing
+claims for the 15 declared rivals remain intact, but the broader “no known
+unresolved defect” statement is superseded by this finite counterexample.
